• Sorting Complex Objects (Comparator.comparing(), .reversed())
Sorts custom Data Transfer Objects (DTOs) by specific attributes using method references and reverse ordering.

• Primitive Stream Conversions (mapToInt(), intStream.average())
Converts object streams into primitive streams to compute numeric metrics like averages without boxing overhead.

• Partitioning vs. Grouping (Collectors.partitioningBy(), Collectors.groupingBy())
Separates data using binary splits (true/false) versus multi-bucket classifications based on a classifier function.

• Downstream Collectors (Collectors.counting(), Collectors.averagingDouble(), Collectors.maxBy())
Combines an initial grouping operation with secondary collectors to aggregate data inside each bucket.

• Map Operations (Map.Entry streams)
Processes, filters, and maps key-value collections generated directly from grouping and partitioning operations.

• Preserving Order (LinkedHashMap supply)
Passes a LinkedHashMap map factory into collectors to maintain original insertion or iteration order during classification.